				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\chi }^{2}\left(1\right)=50.77, p<0.001,\Delta AIC=48.77$$\end{document}χ21=50.77,p<0.001,ΔAIC=48.77). However, synesthetes’ “no color” letters were still surprisingly consistent: test–retest consistency for “no color” letters was not significantly worse than the 135.3 classic threshold for diagnosing synesthesia (Fig. 4; estimated marginal means; \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
